  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_64f4e223176f42c0b87312fb23b3dc66",
      "statement": "RpcGateway is the JSON-RPC composition root: it mounts one UseFramework per alias, wrapping each in its own Catalog (which builds the root bus when the instance was never initialized), so several bounded contexts run in one process; per-alias include/exclude/wrap policies are applied to that alias's catalog only, and re-adding an existing alias replaces its catalog rather than duplicating it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L47-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5d2625e90df60b2d01b5478cb93efa9a34372082a5de4014df26bc2bd6348d2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/entrypoint.py#L64-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc465c4e9878b59893d089e84d7bdb9bdf1bb27458b43ccbe63f3cd0137cf2eb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_83e9fe4e9d3546f9bdd59c419f18080f",
      "statement": "The composition-root alias is not the UseFramework logger name: alias is the mapping key that becomes the method namespace prefix, and validate_alias rejects anything outside ^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$ — notably an alias containing a dot, which would make the instance.layer.Dto split ambiguous.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/entrypoint_rpc.md#L44-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05446c227949fe24455cf5ad450eb7554d7b783c4de5802ed035edd6897d05dd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/entrypoint.py#L24-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20fa43a651ca3e9152e8930f3d1d4120041763bc5b2c0e612538a7e218efd8bc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aaf05a2b4e8d4656aa2ca70d7f45506b",
      "statement": "Published method names are exactly {alias}.{layer}.{DtoName}, composed by method_name; index_methods builds the lookup name -> (alias, UseFramework, PackedFeatureOrAppService) by asking each alias's Catalog for get_scalar_use_cases(filter_binaries_schema=True) and dropping operations whose layer is not in the gateway's configured layers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/entrypoint.py#L51-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:756ac7a5da610250c439dd6723ee8cb66d5344382409cbdf5f8c1aa441e643b4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/jrpc.py#L23-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:951f8b06563d61412720a64dfca708154e7337c2734e7929968e3820975c70b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a2aa79b0fbb34e949ebf59d3ad63b05a",
      "statement": "The methods index and the DTO JSON Schemas behind it are not cached: methods() recomputes index_methods and is called again by both handle() and discover(), so every request and every discovery read rewalks the bus registries.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/entrypoint.py#L99-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bba685b22dd0f17e051b5ced54f96105394761f38fefbcb3c11b53dd84ca10e3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c7829b4b90f444e7af4975a29155a3d4",
      "statement": "The default published surface is both bus layers, because DEFAULT_LAYERS is (Layer.APP_SERVICES, Layer.FEATURES) and Layer is a StrEnum whose only members are \"features\" and \"app_services\"; passing layers=(\"app_services\",) narrows the surface to ApplicationServices.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/const.py#L5-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4de21352f8c9f8c7059d4f6e6b977b70ffa47fb04459648ee2759c97095feb6f:"
        },
        {
