        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6137d2697dea4e7c9497f50fb7007a39",
      "statement": "Batch semantics: a JSON list is a batch, an empty list is invalid and answered with a single -32600 \"Batch must not be empty\" object (not a list), the None replies of notifications are filtered out of the batch result, and a batch whose items were all notifications returns None.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/jrpc.py#L138-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52365046dedc0280d943bcd64b5f7583a566056ae019c1edc2a5f43c99909704:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bac67136a5774400a8708494b8a755c8",
      "statement": "The JSON-RPC request envelope is validated in one place: a request that is not an object, a missing or wrong jsonrpc member, a method that is not a non-empty string, and a context member that is present but not an object all yield -32600 Invalid request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/jrpc.py#L103-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:091be9358f2e011ded3554cf6279b2f44fc95fc42bde0b691fcd310abf8e4979:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cc8c490126a94b73a367cb4ef4908037",
      "statement": "Error and result envelopes have a fixed shape: jsonrpc_error emits {jsonrpc: \"2.0\", id, error: {code, message}} and adds data only when data is not None; jsonrpc_result emits {jsonrpc: \"2.0\", id, result} with the request's own id.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/jrpc.py#L50-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:60e9f855cac8a445e06f49ef8d8e31d3db0e1626952cdd760b60d18eadfeae17:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_737a1d4ea22245359b98f7661dd35c68",
      "statement": "rpc.discover is a real JSON-RPC method on the same dispatch path, and dispatch_method returns the OpenRPC document before validating params or consulting the methods index — so a params array sent to rpc.discover is ignored rather than rejected. RpcGateway.handle() passes its own discover as the discovery callable, so in-process callers, POST /rpc and GET /openrpc.json all return the same document.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/entrypoint.py#L102-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b60bf822a38d99edaf800b432311d58def1a33d7c627238886261997d0b78961:"
