    {
      "id": "claim_3493af8b8b2946e9a076befb729b81b7",
      "statement": "merge_http_context folds transport headers into the inherited framework context without touching DTO params: X-Correlation-Id becomes correlation_id and the W3C traceparent header becomes {\"carrier\": {\"traceparent\": ...}} for OTel parent adoption, while a request with no such headers yields {} rather than a fabricated context.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/entrypoint.py#L34-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d64a1ce695896ef3999e7240e7dae8634ff2dbe4630f4f9bd35a0cee29f9d4b2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/entrypoint/test_entrypoint_rpc.py#L363-L397",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d9f6f40c3893a2dadbb17e0037a6f52478a653c67421c3a822f75cb5720147d9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dce83562ac4f4e409e469354031ab668",
      "statement": "Request-body context wins over headers: handle_single copies the inherited (header-derived) dict first and then updates it with the request's context member, and passes the merged dict down as `merged or None`. context is a sibling of params in the request object, never a DTO field, so a context key cannot collide with a DTO field.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/rpc/jrpc.py#L112-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7dd1603e60a9c00212004166cd507e2d348ae5413c965041dd3e801658d5b46:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/entrypoint/test_entrypoint_rpc.py#L373-L391",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:37091497201d07341e16ec9f9bf850988f579165d46480f7a69d80127f93fc92:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9e65b3c6e56549ed9c1ec8a5b60ccbb1",
      "statement": "The merged context is split by scalar_executor.execute: TRACE_KEYS (\"trace_id\", \"span_id\", \"carrier\") go to framework.with_trace(**trace_kwargs) and the remaining keys to framework.context(extra), each entered only when it has content — so a request carrying only X-Correlation-Id enters a context block and no trace block, while traceparent enters a trace block that adopts the remote parent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/const.py#L18-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:21396ce6d44d87d2b90376271e2a149cc098b8eb16172d99bcca1f5bf24a9daa:"
        },
        {
